      "side": 1,
      "message": "The terminology might be a bit off/confusing here (which I should have noticed in the previous CL).\n\nI don\u0027t think NIST specify an encoding format, just the algorithms and curves.  So I generally use \"NIST\" to refer to the non-Ed25519 curves, whose signatures can either be encoded as a DER structure (e.g. for X.509) or as raw R|S (e.g. for `CoseSign1`). \n\n(However, this distinction has been made less helpful by NIST.FIPS.186-4 getting overtaken by NIST.FIPS.186-5 in 2023/2024, because the latter now includes EdDSA.)",
